  "notes": "The architect of new jack swing; the research windows him **1990–1999 only** for Gate 2, excluding his 1987–89 origin era, and that window is used verbatim. Tempo is \"70–101 straight, swung\", mode 100. The single most load-bearing parameter is the swing itself, and the research states it in mechanical terms: the feel is **\"offbeat-accented 16th-note triplets — a shuffled 16th grid, not straight\"**. That is a full triplet, so `swing.amount` is 0.667 on a 16th grid — the only model in this section at the triplet limit, and far past the genre's 0.62. The other deltas are gear-and-placement claims: \"TR-808 (snare especially prominent), Roland R-8, LinnDrum, SP-1200\" gives a snare stack with a 114–127 accent tier, \"kick doubled on the 16th before 2\" puts the secondary anchor on `1a` (nothing else in this section uses it except his own Blackstreet vehicle), and \"hats crisp and busy\" gives a 0.78 fill density with open hats on three offbeats and a triplet-weighted roll vocabulary. Harmony is the interview's own claim and it is the identifying parameter: he plays by ear with intervals \"way different\" from trained keyboardists, producing chords other musicians could not name — so `topVoiceStepwise` is off, `adjacentSecondProb` is 0.35 for the cluster voicings, the extension spread is seventh-and-ninth heavy over both minor and major tonics, and `halfStepDissonance` is high on the melody. \"Talkbox/vocoder used as a melodic-percussive third voice\" is the counter at a 0.62 density; the bass is \"heavy plucked synth bass with root-fifth two-bar figures, mixed loud\", so root-fifth cells with a mid root-follow. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are all velocity, density and jitter numbers and `adjacentSecondProb` 0.35 — \"unnameable\" is a description, and 0.35 is this author's reading of it. ⚠ `session.keys` is part-sourced: the entry names `F`, and the remaining values `Db`, `Dm`, `Bbm`, `Ab`, together with all 5 weights, are INFERRED rather than read from the entry.",
